summary: The user requested verification of the Daylight task board: build a fresh artifact, read the current app, and verify add, edit, delete, completion, All/Active/Completed filters, empty states, task counts, and reload persistence using concrete assertions that match actual controls. The user explicitly corrected the assertion strategy: target the intended filter controls explicitly rather than clicking whichever filter already has aria-pressed=true, and noted that with one active and one completed task, neither filtered list should be empty. The harness now supports packaged Next stylesheets and client-side React form submit handlers. Current source files were read: app/page.js uses window.askkArtifact.storage with localStorage fallback, app/globals.css includes .storage-error, next.config.js uses output: "export", and package.json uses next 16.3.6 with react 19.3.0. A fresh artifact was built: artifact-fb97150d-802d-4ab4-86ce-07bc2e6f8159, revision 21, status ready, build exitCode 0. Two workspace_check runs against this artifact both failed with ok:false and error "Expected text at .task-title" at index 3 (the first assertText after adding a task), with only indices 0-2 passing. The assertion plan used button[aria-pressed="true"] for filter clicks, which the user identified as incorrect. The assertion plan needs to be revised to explicitly target the All/Active/Completed filter buttons (e.g., by their text content or specific selectors) and re-run workspace_check against the delivered revision until it passes.

